THROWAWAY patch from the real-world memory spike of 2026-11-04, variant FMM: never merge.
It applies to 296ad44 (#559) with `patch -p1` or `git apply`.
The free list mmaps every rgw_max_chunk_size block off the Go heap and munmaps it where it
drops it (over the cap, when shedding, at the trim), with no FreeOSMemory for those; a
forgotten block leaks; blocks of other sizes stay on the Go heap. It exports
rgw_go_memory_budget_free_list_{mmap,munmap}_bytes_total.

